[ ] Specify the cheap coordination pilot protocol =collective-agency-protocol $Apply knowledge/decisions/coordination-pilot-and-trust-limits.md. Predeclare a short two-harness/two-linked-worktree pilot using existing Git, shared claims, checkpoints and handoff documents, not unbuilt entities. Define task, stop budget, independent checks and bounded reconstruction comparison. Required reliance outputs: useful current support reused without rereading, changed support re-observed before action, and measured maintenance cost versus avoided reconstruction with uncertainty explicit. Include duplication, missed dependencies, ownership/activity and global-intent interference, wrong-but-current belief, honest impossibility and peer scope expansion. Corrupt-record probes use disposable state only; distinguish file mismatch from unprovable claimed perception. No standing three-arm study; obtain owner scope/spend approval before execution.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-09-14T10:19 <collective-agency-review #01a0a0ee-331e-7393-8155-5026150db00c
[ ] Pilot coordination with existing tools and measure reliance =coordination-pilot $Run the approved collective-agency-protocol after contextual-freshness per knowledge/decisions/coordination-pilot-and-trust-limits.md. Use two harnesses, linked worktrees, existing Git/claims/checkpoints and handoff documents. Required outputs: measured successor reliance, changed-support response, maintenance-versus-reconstruction cost and uncertainty. Map each duplication, dependency miss, wrong/stale reliance, human recap, ownership/activity or intent-collision gap to a candidate slice or none. Existing tools sufficing is success. If attribution makes failures unscorable, stop and record evidence for the allowed workstreams-first exception; explicitly revise the graph rather than bypass predecessors.$ !2 ^2026-09-14T14:28 <contextual-freshness <collective-agency-protocol #01a0a1d2-318f-76a3-b3d7-4bb8ef380c63
